title: 'pallet-scheduler: place retries with a zero period into the next block'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A retry configured with a `period` of zero is now placed into the next block instead of the
    agenda of the current block, where it was overwritten when that agenda was written back.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    A retry configuration set with `set_retry` or `set_retry_named` and a `period` of zero now
    retries the task in the next block. Before, such a retry never ran.
crates:
- name: pallet-scheduler
  bump: patch
